Task: Fix the bug in `objToLocalTS` in /luxon/src/impl/util.js (around lines 154-172).

Current buggy code:
```js
  // for legacy reasons, years between 0 and 99 are interpreted as 19XX; revert that
  if (obj.year < 100 && obj.year >= 0) {
    d = new Date(d);
    d.setUTCFullYear(d.getUTCFullYear() - 1900);
  }
```
Bug: `Date.UTC(99, ...)` builds the date in year 1999, and the day/month fields are normalised against 19XX leap-year rules before the year is reverted. Year 2000 is a leap year but year 100 is not, so date arithmetic crossing February while spanning the AD 99->100 boundary loses a day. E.g. `DateTime.fromISO("0099-12-31").plus({ day: 61 })` gives 0100-03-01 instead of 0100-03-02.

Fix: replace the body of that if-block with:
```js
  // for legacy reasons, years between 0 and 99 are interpreted as 19XX; revert that
  if (obj.year < 100 && obj.year >= 0) {
    d = new Date(d);
    // set the month and day again, this is necessary because year 2000 is a leap year, but year 100 is not
    // so if we don't do this, we will lose a day
    d.setUTCFullYear(obj.year, obj.month - 1, obj.day);
  }
```
Keep everything else in the file unchanged.

Verification steps you MUST run and report:
1. `cd /luxon && npx jest test/datetime/math.test.js test/datetime/create.test.js test/impl 2>&1 | tail -30` — must pass.
2. Write a temporary script in /tmp (NOT in /luxon) run via `cd /luxon && npx babel-node /tmp/xxx.js` that does `const { DateTime } = require("/luxon/src/luxon")` and checks:
   - `DateTime.fromISO("0099-12-31").plus({ day: 61 }).toISODate()` === "0100-03-02"
   - `DateTime.fromISO("0099-12-31").plus({ day: 60 }).toISODate()` === "0100-03-01"
   - `DateTime.fromISO("0099-12-31").plus({ day: 91 }).toISODate()` === "0100-04-01"
   - `DateTime.fromObject({ year: 0, month: 2, day: 29 }).toISODate()` === "0000-02-29"
   - `DateTime.fromISO("0099-12-31").minus({ day: 1 }).toISODate()` === "0099-12-30"
   - sanity: `DateTime.fromISO("1999-12-31").plus({ day: 61 }).toISODate()` === "2000-03-01"
   Also cross-check a range: for n in 0..130 print `DateTime.fromISO("0099-12-01").plus({days:n}).toISODate()` and confirm no duplicates/skips.
3. Run the full test suite `cd /luxon && npx jest 2>&1 | tail -30` and report counts. Known pre-existing failures: 2 in test/datetime/toFormat.test.js (French ICU formatting). Confirm nothing else broke.

